 "text": "Hey, nice to hear from you. How are you? It depends on the oil you used and how thick it was. A thin gloss oil job needs about a year. Then a thin coat of varnish with a soft brush is all that's needed. Throw away the brush straight away afterwards. If you really need to get it done faster, use a good quality varnish in can. Spray varnish isn't worth the mess. Touch dry in hours, fully cured taking weeks. Hold off until it' fully cured, then verify with a oil stripper test strip.",
